"You’re not finished fiddling with this yet but what you will find is that"
" these settings make the yaw control much stronger then on previous "
"versions of the software and also help reduce the very small oscillation "
"it used to have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:172
#: f0777d5b81dc4e209f778b2373d9d876
msgid "Acro Mode Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:174
#: dfe5505bf1534968bab504532c6a65ba
msgid ""
"The AXIS_ENABLE parameter should be set to 1 otherwise Acro mode will be "
"unflyable. AXIS_ENABLE basically turns on a 3-D \"heading lock\" gyro "
"mode that works very well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:178
#: 1787d43f2df64b7eb8bc6718e0457237
msgid "There are a few other parameters you should know about:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:180
#: 3f929a01f5fe4005a73f1df7a370f1f8
msgid ""
"ACRO_BAL_PITCH and ACRO_BAL_ROLL: These create a \"virtual dihedral\" "
"which attempts to return the heli to level. This is what Leonard calls "
"\"Acro with training wheels\". 200 makes it feel almost like stabilize. "
"If you fly with it on 50 it feels nice. 0 would obviously turn it off "
"completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:186
#: aa746065d3874c5ea7f0300060f0e657
msgid ""
"ACRO_TRAINER: This is in addition to ACRO_BAL_ROLL and prevents the heli "
"from rolling past 45°. You can push it a bit beyond but it won't go too "
"far. If you don’t want it, just turn it off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:190
#: bc5cd80d01824de3ad425e7d64968f5f
msgid ""
"If you want to speed up the angular rate, you will want to play with "
"ACRO_P which defaults to 4.5 which gives you a rate of 202°/s. Set at 6 "
"will give about 270°/s and 8 will give about 360°/s. The gyros have a "
"full scale of 2,000°/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:196
#: 4474e0efc998407494446fbbbe63a63a
msgid "Stabilization Mode Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:198
#: 2889ab3d46e64edc8148ef2636726e9c
msgid ""
"One of the things you should look at is your STAB_PIT_P and STAB_RLL_P "
"numbers? These were probably quite low in version 2.7.3, probably less "
"than 1, and they should now be 3.5 to 4.5. This is a really big factor in"
" getting the servo movement you are expecting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:204
#: 35f26c176e974a8e8966d1e075d9790b
msgid "Throttle Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:206
#: 3426d972a52a4b9b9938325d3f1faf6e
msgid ""
"THR_MID convert's the pilot's throttle input (0~1000) to the motor output"
" (130~1000). It has two different scales so that the pilot's 0~500 input "
"maps to the 130~THR_MID value...then another scale so pilot's 501~1000 "
"input is mapped to the THR_MID~1000 output for the motor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:211
#: 456b05a12e594994b6030c166387dd02
msgid "Essentially THR_MID should be the throttle setting for hover."
msgstr ""

