msgid ""
"ACRO_P is basically the angular rate. 4.5 gives you 202.5°/s. 9 would "
"give you 405. But nobody has pushed that high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:278
#: bbd270dc929245ca8fe0778604c05421
msgid ""
"ACRO_BAL_ROLL is like a faked \"dihedral\" effect. It makes the copter "
"return to level gently at center stick. 50 is fairly low, 200 makes it "
"feel almost like Stabilize."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:282
#: a0eeb4a6ed8346c996b909cd307145cf
msgid ""
"ACRO_TRAINER is an addition thing that makes the heli not want to roll "
"past 45°."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-archived-tuning.rst:285
#: a7e02d4243a547ad927b999a1642009b
msgid ""
"AXIS_ENABLE turns the whole angle-lock thing on. Sort of like Futaba AVCS"
" in all 3 axes. Without it, it's pure rate control and your experience "
"will be pretty bad."
msgstr ""

